    "q-250665": {
      "dom_id": "step-q250665",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n-4,\\,16,\\,-64,\\,256,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe fifth term of this sequence is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14225716/assets/84c714b0c37c7f28cb83c59e3455755470ff6aa69da145c80ccea19200b1ad8f.png)\n\nNotice that the sequence is geometric, with a common ratio of \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{16}{(-4)}=-4.\n$$\n\nSo, we can get each term by multiplying the previous term by $-4.$ \n\nContinuing to list terms of the sequence until we get to the $5$th term, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14225716/assets/400ef822bd63631f65a4190f8367e84878c03a302c3202a112e9de2858ae4249.png)\n\nTherefore, the $5$th term is $-1\\,024.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
